// SPDX-License-Identifier: CECILL-2.1
//
// Model-fixture parity tests for the core regression-solver PLS families that
// are reachable through the public `n4m_model_fit` / `n4m_model_predict` /
// `n4m_model_get_array` C ABI.
//
// Each family's expected coefficients / preprocessing stats / latent matrices /
// training predictions are read from the mechanically generated fixture headers
// under cpp/tests/fixtures/ (regenerated by
// parity/python_generator/src/pls4all_parity/cpp_header.py). Every generated
// family header shares the same record layout (id, n_components, X, Y,
// coefficients, intercept, x_mean, x_scale, y_mean, y_scale, weights_w,
// loadings_p, y_loadings_q, rotations_r, scores_t, predict_train) so a single
// templated checker drives all of them — only the (algorithm, solver,
// deflation) config triple changes between families.
//
// Tolerance: the solver/algorithm rows in parity/tolerances.md gate these at
// abs/rel 1e-9 (`pls4all-numpy-{simpls,svd,power,randomized-svd}`,
// `sklearn/PLSCanonical/*`, `sklearn/PLSSVD`, `sklearn/PLSDA-dummy`,
// `pls4all-numpy-{opls,opls-da-*,kernelpls,wide-kernelpls,pcr}`,
// `pls-r-oscorespls`). Latent matrices (weights/loadings/scores/rotations) are
// only determined up to a per-column sign, so the generator marks them
// sign_invariant and the checker compares magnitudes for those.

